## Features Being Tested

### Feature 1 - Login and Access Library

#### Acceptance Criterion 1

Given a user has created an account, when they enter valid login credentials, then they should be successfully logged into the application.

#### UAT Scenario

You've used TookABook before and want to access your library.

#### Task

Sign in and access your books.

#### Expected Result

The participant successfully signs in and can access their library.

--- 

#### Acceptance Criterion 2

Given a user is logged in, when they access their library, then they should only see books associated with their account.

#### UAT Scenario

You would like to check that your personal library contains the books you've uploaded.

#### Task

Find and review the books available in your account.

#### Expected Result

Only books belonging to the participant's account are visible.


--- 

#### Acceptance Criterion 3

Given a user enters incorrect login credentials, when they attempt to log in, then an appropriate error message should be displayed.

#### UAT Scenario

You accidentally entered the wrong password when trying to access your account.

#### Task

Attempt to sign in using incorrect account details.

#### Expected Result

An error message is displayed, and access is denied.

--- 

### Feature 2 - Upload Books

#### Acceptance Criterion 1

Given that a user is logged in, when they try to upload a book or PDF, the app should display a success alert.

#### UAT Scenario

You've got a book on your device that you'd like to keep in TookABook so you can read it later.

#### Task

Add the book to your library.

#### Expected Result

The participant successfully uploads the book and receives confirmation that it was added.

--- 

#### Acceptance Criterion 2

Given a user is logged in, when they attempt to upload an unsupported file type, then the application should display an error message and prevent the upload.

#### UAT Scenario

You accidentally selected a file that isn't a book format supported by the app.

#### Task

Try to add the file to your library.

#### Expected Result

The upload is rejected, and an error message explains why.

--- 
